{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>I have seen.</b> The meaning of ורעות רוח is like \"Ephraim is a feeder of wind, and pursues the east wind\" — which does not profit and does not satisfy. And the matter of רוח is like הבל, because of the abundance of its goings, that a person cannot grasp it in his hand, like the matter of \"for wind they sow\" and likewise \"for a wind passed over it.\" And it is possible that ורעות is like מחשבת, and it indicates רעיון רוח, and their pattern is דמות and דמיון, from the verbs whose lamed is not complete."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The verse quoted elliptically as 'for wind they sow' and 'for a wind passed over it' likely alludes to Hosea 8:7 and one of several possible verses (e.g. Jonah 4:8 or Isaiah 40:7); the precise second citation is uncertain among witnesses."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:49.369358472Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}